setDate ← setDateTimePickerValue ← applyUnavailableDates ← resolveWith ← (XMLHttpRequest.send) ← send ← ajax ← getUnavailableDates ← (setTimeout) ← onMonthChange ← setDate
```

This indicates that the `setDate` flag passed to `applyUnavailableDates` is `true` (because it comes from `getUnavailableDates` which calls `applyUnavailableDates(..., true)` in the `onMonthChange` handler).

In our override, we tried to set `setDate = false` when the user has typed a date. However, note that the `applyUnavailableDates` function is also responsible for greying out unavailable dates. We must still perform that action, just not change the date.

